    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2009961595238269437",
      "url": "https://x.com/investor_sr33/status/2009961595238269437",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/investor_sr33/status/2009961595238269437",
      "text": "Today is my dad’s birthday.\nI just wanted to write this—no filters.\n\nHe was an IIT Roorkee MTech, a chemical engineer.\nLeft a secure government job and chose entrepreneurship.\n\nHe started Lucast Chemicals in the mid-80s.\nManufactured copper sulphate.\nTook a ₹5 lakh KSFC loan.\nWas allotted 2 acres in Electronic City—back when it was just land and hope.\n\nEntrepreneurship wasn’t glamorous then.\nLosses.\nTheft at the factory.\nStress that never switched off.\n\nHe smoked 2–3 packs a day.\nLived under pressure.\nAnd in 1996, he passed away—right in front of me.\nCardiac arrest. Multiple organ failure.\n\nSome truths are harsh:\nEntrepreneurship isn’t for everyone.\nStress kills faster than failure.\n\nAfter he was gone, his so-called partners walked away.\nThe entire debt was pushed onto us.\nWe ended up paying ₹40 lakhs with interest, finally closing it in 2006.\n\nWhat saved us?\nMy mother’s job. Her strength. Her stability.\n\nOne lesson I’ll never forget:\nAlways educate girls. It helps them stand on their own.\n\nLife is unpredictable.\nHealth truly is wealth.\nDreams are important—but so is sleeping peacefully at night.\n\nToday, I don’t glorify struggle.\nI respect it.\nAnd I choose balance.\n\nBe healthy.\nBe responsible.\nBe happy.\n\nThat’s the real success.",
